    "summary": "Fire‑filled set with Dark Star, China>Rider and strong second half",
    "blurb": "The Boston Garden show delivers a scorching second set highlighted by Dark Star, China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider and a punchy New Speedway Boogie. Jerry’s guitar soars after a slower first set, while Bruce Hornsby adds lush keyboards throughout.",
    "review": "On September 24, 1991 the Dead took Boston Garden by storm. The first set opened with solid roots material—Let The Good Times Roll and Althea—but it was the second half that truly ignited the crowd. A blistering China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue showcased Jerry’s “crazy midi‑fied” solos, and the ensuing Dark Star unfolded with relentless energy. Highlights continued with Ship Of Fools, Foolish Heart, and a soaring Standing On The Moon that rescued any early‑set sluggishness. The night closed on a high note with New Speedway Boogie and a heartfelt Weight encore.\n\nBruce Hornsby’s keyboard textures are repeatedly praised for their “psychedelic bayou” flavor, though one listener noted Vince Welnick’s playing as overly cheesy. Overall the show is considered one of the stronger entries in the 1991 Boston run, especially for fans chasing that fiery second‑set vibe.",
